    {
      "id": "section:11/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "**System Management Interrupts (SMIs)** are generated by the BIOS/UEFI and run in System Management Mode (SMM) — completely invisible to the OS and cannot be disabled by the kernel ([Intel SDM Vol. 3, Chapter 34](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-sdm.html)):",
      "source_hash": 2261592221597358039,
      "context_hash": 15167412224787173142,
      "translation": "**시스템 관리 인터럽트**(System Management Interrupts, SMI)는 BIOS/UEFI가 생성하며 시스템 관리 모드(System Management Mode, SMM)에서 실행됩니다 — OS에서는 전혀 보이지 않으며 커널이 비활성화할 수도 없습니다([Intel SDM Vol. 3, Chapter 34](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/intel-sdm.html)):",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Intel": "Intel",
        "interrupt": "인터럽트"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:33:05.701665Z",
      "issues": []
